# All sessions, all repos

Standing operator ruling: **every** Cursor session (local and Cloud) and **every** product repo (existing and new) operates under JHD discipline. No exceptions for “quick Cloud fixes.”

## Existing repos
Must carry committed Cloud-portable discipline:
- `AGENTS.md`
- `.cursor/rules/` from plugin SoT `rules/` (invariants, routing, cloud-first, operator-voice, all-sessions) plus product overlay when applicable

Sync with `scripts/sync-discipline-into-product.sh <path> <kind>` (Mac) whenever `rules/` or templates change. Commit inside each product repo.

## New repos
Before the first agent session (local or Cloud):
1. Run `scripts/sync-discipline-into-product.sh <path> product` (or the matching kind from `config/jhd-repos.json`).
2. Commit `AGENTS.md` + `.cursor/rules/`.
3. Ensure the GitHub App can see the new remote (Environment token includes vault + discipline).

## Every session
- Wrong-repo Cloud/local session → stop; open/start the correct product-repo session.
- Missing in-repo rules on Cloud → treat as incomplete setup; sync/commit before claiming discipline is active.
- Discipline-only workspace is for plugin maintenance — never for Capture/portfolio/product implementation.
- Vault absent on Cloud → say so once; still follow in-repo rules.

## Session open (every product-repo session, including summarised/continued chats)
- **MUST** read vault `projects/<name>/<name>-handover.md` (infer project from workspace) then `orchestrator/cockpit.md`.
- **Do not rely on conversation summary or transcript summary as continuity SoT.** After summary injection / continued chat, re-read project handover before dispatch or wrap claims. Transcript summary ≠ handover.
- Never use generic `HANDOVER.md` — unique handover stems only (`unique-note-names`).
- **Leftover (`leftover-not-a-board`):** read handover Open at session start for product still-open; this chat's lock is in vs missing. Surface leftover on ask, at wrap, after PASS — not every turn. transcript summary ≠ leftover.
- Load `vault-recall` / handover command behaviour when resuming.

## Session end (wrap / hand over / continue fresh, or non-trivial product work closing)
- **MUST** read `skills/wrap/SKILL.md` and execute all seven sections + learn + lint + estate sync + push.
- **MUST NOT** tell the operator "partial wrap is enough." Partial handover alone is a **routing failure**.
- Durable vault writes during orchestration → read and follow `vault-write`; ad-hoc vault Write without that skill is a defect (the Write tool is still how vault-write authors notes).

## Done / "fixed" (every session — not optional)
- Engineer completion ≠ done. Orchestrator **must not** relay engineer "done" / "fixed" / "parity" to the operator.
- After engineer lands → dispatch **reviewer**. Only **reviewer PASS** may be reported as done.
- Do **not** report ready-to-look until **`present-for-review`** has run when a live product exists — screenshot, "go look," or a spawned Browser window is not presentation.
- Look/feel / match Figma / match reference → **ux-designer** for agent evidence; operator packet is **`present-for-review`** after PASS; reviewer **BLOCK**s diff-only visual claims.
- **Forbidden:** Skipping reviewer because the change is "routine", "one file", or "discipline/docs". Routine PRs skip the **operator merge click**, not reviewer.

## Baton (parent-only Task — completion notification)
- **Only the orchestrator `Task`s.** Specialists never `Task` another specialist — they land, name the next owner in evidence, and stop.
- On completion notification: engineer landed → parent **`Task`s reviewer**; reviewer **BLOCK** → parent **`Task`s engineer** (`resume`) with gaps; look/feel or missing render → parent **`Task`s ux-designer** for agent evidence; reviewer **PASS** → parent loads **`present-for-review`** when a live product exists, then remits merge (engineer or releaseops).
- Parent default **`run_in_background`** and **end the turn** after dispatch — do not AwaitShell/poll the specialist.
- Parent is **not a waiting room**. Silence **after the completion ping** is a routing failure. Waiting **inside** the dispatch turn is also a routing failure.
- **`ignore-resume-toast`:** Resume / *Error resuming chat* after a background specialist → **ignore**; not leftover; parent `Task`s next owner on completion ping. Never operator Resume homework. Plugin cannot suppress Cursor UI.

## Plugin updates sync everywhere (`plugin-update-syncs-everywhere`)

A plugin version bump is **unfinished** until `scripts/sync-discipline-all-repos.sh` has committed `AGENTS.md` + `.cursor/rules` in every registered product checkout. Cloud/plugin-off sessions only get what each repo last committed — stale overlays are the defect. Sync discipline-only paths; never mix product WIP into overlay commits.

## Cursor Environment (fleet)
Token access: **`jhd-cursor-discipline` + `jhd-vault`**. New product remote → ensure the GitHub App can see it; do **not** add every product as a selected checkout on the Environment card.
